Package: HypoShrink
Type: Package
Title: Companion Hypothesis Matrices for Quadratic-Form-Based Tests
Version: 0.0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Paavo", "Sattler",
           email = "paavo.sattler@tu-dortmund.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8731-0893")),
    person("Manuel", "Rosenbaum",
           role = "ctb")
)
Description: A collection of functions to compute so-called companion
    hypotheses for given linear hypotheses. Companion hypotheses provide
    minimal-row representations while preserving the relevant quadratic-form
    structure. For variants of the ANOVA-type statistic (ATS), suitable
    companion constructions preserve the corresponding statistic values.
    Related invariance results are available for the Wald-type statistic
    (WTS) and the modified ANOVA-type statistic (MATS) under the respective
    regularity conditions. Reducing the number of rows can substantially
    decrease computational effort. Companion hypotheses can be obtained
    numerically or, in the case of the centering matrix, via an explicit
    formula. For methodological details, see Sattler and Rosenbaum (2025).
